These sounds are the "zen" pack from uisfx by Romain Simon:
https://github.com/romainsimon/uisfx, commit 9950fe6
(packages/uisfx/sounds/zen/*.ogg).

They are dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0 (see LICENSE-AUDIO,
copied unchanged from packages/uisfx/LICENSE-AUDIO).

Changes made for Xidou Shell:
- Only the 59 cues mapped in docs/ROADMAP.md section 7 are kept. The other
  19 are left out.
- Each .ogg was converted once to 16-bit PCM WAV with the same sample rate
  and channels, because Qt's SoundEffect plays WAV only. The same +9.5 dB gain
  was applied to every cue during the conversion: the pack's files peak around
  -11 dBFS, and +9.5 dB puts the loudest one (drag-start) at -1.08 dBFS with
  no clipped samples, without changing the balance between cues:
  `ffmpeg -i <cue>.ogg -map_metadata -1 -fflags +bitexact
  -af volume=9.5dB:precision=double -c:a pcm_s16le <cue>.wav`
- cues.json holds each cue's loop flag and default volume. `upstream_volume`
  is copied from the pack's manifest.json (the same values as
  src/catalog.ts's CUES table). `volume`, the value Xidou uses, is
  upstream_volume x 1.5 for every cue. Upstream's values all sit at or below
  0.26, which left a 100% setting quiet with no way up. Scaling all of them by
  one factor keeps their ratios.
